    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/Winona/Assistant-to-the-President---Provost--Office---Admin-Specialist-Senior-_JR0000005631": {
      "title": "Assistant to the President & Provost (Office & Admin Specialist Senior)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant to the President & Provost (Office & Admin Specialist Senior) Institution: Winona State University Classification Title: Office & Admin Specialist Sr Bargaining Unit / Union: 217: Non-Represented Employee Plan City: Winona FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $22.62 - $32.23 Job Description To provide senior level administrative support and assistance to the President and Provost and assist the office Executive Assistant II in managing the President’s Office and Office of Academic Affairs. This position must maintain confidentiality when processing information, data, and budgets that pertain to collective bargaining and labor relation decisions related to Minnesota State Colleges and Universities and Winona State University.  The reports, data, and information defined by M.S. 13.37 accessed in this position can be used in collective bargaining proposals, to make labor relations and decisions at the system level, the local level, or to settle grievances.   Responsibilities: 1. Provide President and Provost with confidential administrative support and collaborate with the Executive Assistant in managing overall functioning of the President’s and Provost’s Office. Serve as the Receptionist for the Office of the President and Provost greeting guests, answering phones and serving as the first point of contact. Screen calls/emails appropriately and assist with inquires.Refer non-routing matters to the appropriate contact in the office. Determine procedures and prioritize to accomplish a variety of work tasks for the President and Provost. Prepare and send correspondence and memos as requested by the President and Provost, including letters of offer, faculty retirement recommendations, department chairs nominations, etc. Coordinate and oversee timely responses from other areas, when appropriate. Establish office procedures and priorities; order and maintain office supplies, using University credit card or Marketplace. Recruit, hire, schedule, and train student office assistants to the professional standard required in the President’s office. Delegate duties and oversee assigned projects. Enter assignment forms for new or interim deans and non-instructional assignments for faculty. Serve as a liaison with students by responding to students via letters, phone calls and emails on issues of personal concerns. Resolve issues and/or recommend a course of action. Serve as a resource person (internally and externally) for university questions regarding Winona state regulations, Minnesota State Colleges and Universities policies, and procedures and other general concerns. Meet with students, procure records, research details as needed to ensure solutions are following university regulations Serve as backup to office Executive Assistant to maintain the President and Provost’s electronic calendars. Schedule appointments. Coordinate and schedule group meetings for both on and off campus. Maintain calendar accuracy on daily basis. Schedule recurring appointments with individuals and groups. Schedule and lead periodic (quarterly) meetings with the Deans Administrative Assistants. Apprise president and provost of campus visitors/guests, events such as Lyceum and other presentations/engagements, athletic competitions, theatre and music performances, Rochester, Winona and area events, etc.   Generate all travel itineraries and accommodations for the President and Provost. Process the necessary forms for timely reimbursement of all expenses. Reconcile the President and Provost’s travel card expenditures monthly, attaching appropriate receipts for payment. Coordinate development and maintenance of the President and Academic Affairs websites. Maintain the office filing system that includes confidential and sensitive information regarding labor relations in accordance with M.S 13.37 and personnel issues, in accordance with the current data privacy law and forms retention schedule. Archive pertinent records on an annual basis. 2. Collaborate with the Executive Assistant serving as a resource to the President’s and Provost’s Office on labor relations/contractual issues as defined under M.S 13.37. Provide support in maintaining confidential labor relations information for the President and Provost’s Office as defined in M.S. 13.37 including but not limited to collective bargaining proposals, strategies, costing information and other labor relations information. Provide assistance to the Executive Assistant in conducting research on various issues to assist with preparation of bargaining materials.Assist in reviewing written proposal to be presented for bargaining. Provide assistance in reviewing and providing feedback on contract provisions/proposals that affect university programs. Compile and update the spreadsheets for the IFO, Adjunct, and Academic Affairs ASF Professional Improvement Funds applications and forward to the office Executive Assistant by the due date. Collect the PIF reports from Deans, ensure the provost signs them, then forward them to the office Executive Assistant. Compile and update the spreadsheets for the IFO and Academic Affairs ASF sabbatical requests. Submit to the office Executive Assistant by the due date. Collect the Sabbatical reports from the Deans, ensure the provost signs them, then forward them to the office Executive Assistant. Complete the annual Sabbatical Report for the System Office. Prepare the IFO Promotion and Tenure files for review by the provost and president. Ensure files are complete and documents are completed as required. Draft and send memos to faculty at the provost’s and president’s direction. Schedule meetings with faculty and the provost and/or the president as requested. Submit the files to the office Executive Assistant by the due date. 3. C ollaborate with Executive Assistant in the coordination and execution of events hosted by the President and/or Provost.  Accept lead work assigned by Executive Assistant to accomplish commencement duties during both fall and spring semesters, Welcome Week, Evening of Distinction events, promotion and tenure celebrations, Pizza with the Presidents, and other university sponsored events. 4. Assists the Provost to Chair the Calendar Committee This position assumes committee chair responsibilities in the absence of the Provost. Prepare two to three years of draft academic calendar. Coordinate, participate in, and record minutes for all meetings of the Calendar Committee Ensure each constituent group on campus receives the calendar to review and comment on prior to a memo being sent by the Provost to the President for final approval. Review Faculty Duty Days calendar as presented by the Faculty Senate to ensure appropriate number of duty days and post the calendar online. Prepare the academic year calendar for inclusion in the University catalogs and posting on the website. Processes are ongoing with three years lead time. 5. Create and distribute Winona State University’s Academic Deadline and Personnel Decision Deadline Calendars.Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor. Update calendars annually to provide a source of reference for pertinent deadline information for faculty, staff, and students. Coordinate and verify dates to be included from Admissions, Registrar’s, Business Office, Graduate Office, Advising Services, WSU Regulations, and WSU policies & procedures. Include personnel decision deadlines imperative to faculty in compliance with the IFO/MnSCU Master Agreement Ensure the Personnel Decision Deadline Calendar has been presented to the IFO at Meet and Confer. Post both Deadline Calendars on the website. Salary Range: $22.62-$32.23/hour; commensurate with qualifications and experience Minimum Qualifications One year of assistant or office manager experience supporting a senior level position.A bachelor’s degree may substitute for one year of experience; an Associate’s degree may substitute for six months of experience.The degree must be in Business Administration, Communications or a related field. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills; ability to interact with diverse populations. Excellent decision-making and critical thinking skills Experience working with highly confidential information. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with administrators, faculty, staff, students, and the public. Strong organizational and multitasking abilities, Demonstrated ability to work with a high degree of autonomy and display self-motivation Incumbent possesses ability to “troubleshoot” situations and skills in conflict resolution. Proficient computer knowledge, including Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, and Outlook to perform accurate and efficient duties related to office management for the President and Provost   Preferred Qualification  Five or more years working in a senior level administrative support role. Bachelor’s degree in Business Management, Communications or related field. Knowledge of State of Minnesota, Minnesota State Colleges and Universities, and Winona State University policies and procedures. Proficiency with Minnesota State Colleges and Universities systems for tracking financial, student and personnel records. Database management experience. Experience working in an academic environment. Experience working in a bargaining unit environment. Demonstrated experience working in a fast-paced environment with competing deadlines. Demonstrated ability to apply excellent decision-making skills, objectivity, compassion, desire and ability to seek solutions that are win-win.   Other Requirements 1. The successful candidate must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States by the day employment begins. The University regrets that we are unable to offer H1-B sponsorship at this time.   2. A complete online application will include the following: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed previously Resume   Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday-Friday; 8:00am-4:30pm Posting Information: Application Deadline: September 16, 2026 Appointment Date: As Soon As Possible Primary Location: Winona, MN Type of Appointment: Probationary Telework (Yes/No) No About Winona State University Founded in 1858, Winona State University is a regional public university and the oldest member of the Minnesota State system. Offering more than 200 majors and programs, Winona State has the #1 Student Success Rate in the Minnesota State System with 96.97 percent of WSU graduates being hired in a field related to their degree. U.S. News recognized Winona State as having top-ranking undergraduate programs in nursing, engineering, psychology, business, and computer science. With campuses in both Winona and Rochester, Winona State offers the best of both worlds. Widely known for its stunning natural setting, the Winona campus is nestled between picturesque bluffs and the Mississippi River - meaning rock climbing, paddle-boarding, hiking, and kayaking are within a mile of campus. WSU’s Rochester campus is located in Minnesota’s third largest city - a dynamic hub for industry, arts, and culture, and consistently ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. Winona State University's mission is to enhance the intellectual, social, cultural and economic vitality of the people and communities we serve: a community of learners improving our world. For more information, visit winona.edu. Notice: In accordance with Minnesota State policy, employees driving on university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a motor vehicle records check. The Winona State University Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school's policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security. Three years' worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at https://www.winona.edu/about/safety-security/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security by emailing security@winona.edu . Winona State University is an Equal Opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. A member of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities System. A community of learners improving our world! Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-27-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-01-2026 Close Date: 09-03-2026 Posting Contact Name: Robin M Delong Posting Contact Email: rdelong@winona.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/Winona/Associate-Vice-President-of-Human-Resources---CHRO--MnSCU-Admin-7-_JR0000005623-1": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President of Human Resources / CHRO (MnSCU Admin-7)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Associate Vice President of Human Resources / CHRO (MnSCU Admin-7) Institution: Winona State University Classification Title: MnSCU Administrator 7 Bargaining Unit / Union: 220: Minnesota State Administrator's Plan City: Winona FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $105,407.00 - $169,114.00 Job Description The Associate Vice President of Human Resources and Chief Human Resources Officer (AVP/CHRO) provides strategic leadership, vision, and direction for all human resources functions across the university. As a key member of the President’s Cabinet, the AVP/CHRO serves as the senior advisor on organizational strategy, workforce planning, labor relations, and employee engagement. This role ensures that HR practices support the university’s mission, values, and long-term goals while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing culture. Responsibilities: 1. Strategic Leadership and HR Vision Provide strategic leadership for all HR functions, establishing short- and long-term goals aligned with the University’s strategic plan and Minnesota State system priorities. Serve as a key advisor to the President, Cabinet, and senior leadership on workforce planning, organizational development, and personnel matters. Participate as a member of the President’s Cabinet and Council of Administrators, contributing to institutional decision-making and daily operations. Represent the University on system-level HR committees and contribute to the development and evaluation of system-wide HR policies and practices. Represent the university on internal committees, ensuring alignment with institutional goals and shared governance principles. Lead continuous improvement efforts to ensure HR operations are efficient, innovative, and responsive to campus needs. 2. Employee and Labor Relations Leadership Serve as the university’s chief labor relations authority, overseeing contract administration, grievance management, arbitration preparation assistance, and resolution of complex employee relations issues. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with union leadership and internal stakeholders to support a productive and respectful work environment. Participate in system-level negotiations teams and contract language review. Partner with Cabinet to lead campus meet and confer processes, including agenda development and follow up, and strike plan preparation; maintain strike plans. Hear complex grievances with the President and senior leaders and advice leadership on sensitive labor matters. 3. HR Operations, Compliance, and Risk Management Oversee all HR functional areas, including classification and compensation, recruitment and selection, workforce planning, performance management, progressive discipline, benefits and leave administration, workers’ compensation, unemployment, HR systems management, payroll, staffing, Affirmative Action, and succession planning. Ensure compliance with federal and state employment laws, Minnesota Management and Budget (MMB) policies, Minnesota State system policies, collective bargaining agreements, and university policies and procedures. Direct the management, retention, and auditing of confidential personnel data, ensuring accuracy, security, and timely reporting to internal and external agencies. Oversee day-to-day HR operations in partnership with the Assistant HR Director to ensure efficient, compliant, and customer-focused service delivery. 4. Organizational Culture, Engagement, and Development Lead initiatives that foster a collaborative, inclusive, and engaging workplace culture that supports employee satisfaction, retention, and development. Oversee professional development programming, leadership and supervisory training, and required employee training. Collaborate with the Assistant Vice President for Equity and Inclusive Excellence on campus climate survey, analyze results, and guide institutional action planning. Champion employee recognition initiatives and collaborate with Marketing to strengthen the university’s employment brand. Encourage innovation by challenging outdated processes and promoting continuous improvement across HR and campus operations. 5. Equity, Inclusion, and Affirmative Action Partnership Collaborate with the Department of Equity and Inclusive Excellence on policies, procedures, and initiatives related to workforce equity, inclusion, and Affirmative Action. Ensure HR practices support equitable hiring, retention, and advancement. Provide leadership on campus wellness initiatives that promote the well-being of all employees. 6. HR Office Leadership and Resource Management Supervise HR staff, providing coaching, performance evaluation, and professional development to ensure effective service delivery. Manage the HR Office budget, staffing, and resource allocation to support strategic and operational priorities. Ensure timely and accurate HCM and payroll processing, resolving pay-related issues in compliance with applicable laws and agreements. 7. Data, Reporting, and External Relations Provide accurate and timely HR data, reports, and analysis to support decision-making, accreditation, audit and legislative requests, and system initiatives. Represent the university in external meetings, hearings, and committees, serving as liaison to the system office, state agencies, and legal counsel on employment matters. Use data-driven insights to guide HR strategy, culture initiatives, and organizational development efforts. 8. Other responsibilities as designated by the VP for Finance & Administration/CFO and University President. The Key Accountabilities Include: Strategic leadership of all human resource functions. Trusted advisor to the President and senior leadership on all matters related to the human resource health of the institution. Lead labor relations authority for the university; coordinate multiple university strike plans. Develop/maintain highly functioning human resource operations compliant with applicable laws and policies. Lead and coordinate organization culture initiatives for a collaborative, inclusive, and engaged workforce. Lead an effective and efficient human resource operation. Timely, accurate, and complete reporting to stakeholders. Coordinate on employment matters serving as a liaison to the system office, state agencies, and legal counsel and represent the university in meetings, hearing, and committees. Strategic contributing member of the President’s cabinet Commitment to ongoing professional development, continued learning and staying current on emerging trends, best practices, employment laws, and human resources issues.   Salary Range: $105,407.00 - $169,114.00 ; Commensurate with qualifications and experience Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or other advanced degree from an accredited institution in human resources, labor relations, employment law, business administration, organizational leadership or related field. Ten (10) years of professional human resource experience in a complex organization. Demonstrated supervisory or managerial experience in human resources. Demonstrated experience and competence in interpreting, applying, and ensuring compliance with federal and state employment laws and organizational policies. Experience with labor relations and collective bargaining agreement administration. Demonstrated organizational leadership and management skills. Demonstrated commitment to inclusiveness in leadership and decision-making. Excellent writing, speaking, and interpersonal skills. Ability to successfully pass a criminal background check and be authorized to review criminal history records information. Preferred Qualification  Professional HR certifications such as Senior Professional in Human Resources (SPHR) or SHRM Senior Certified Professional (SHRM-SCP). Demonstrated knowledge across multiple HR functions to include labor relations, workforce planning, compensation and classification, recruitment, leave management, benefits administration, employee relations, performance management, training and development, HRIS, workers’ compensation, unemployment insurance, and affirmative action. Experience in public sector human resources. Experience working in human resources in a medium or large organization with complex operations. Experience interpreting policy and labor agreements, handling complaint resolution and grievance processes. Experience in mediation or conflict resolution. Demonstrated experience building and maintaining constructive business relationships with union representatives. Experience in higher education. Ability to work effectively and collegially within a large, complex university system and to negotiate with a wide range of constituencies, including multiple bargaining units. Demonstrated ability to provide strategic vision in complex organizations. Demonstrated success in budget planning and creative problem solving to advance organization initiatives. Demonstrated proficiency and ability to use technology to develop efficient business processes.   Other Requirements 1. The successful candidate must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States by the day employment begins. The University regrets that we are unable to offer H1-B sponsorship at this time. 2. A complete online application will include the following: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed previously Current Curriculum Vitae / Resume Transcripts (undergraduate and graduate) A list of professional references with contact information   Posting Information: Application Deadline: Priority consideration given to applications received by September 28, 2026 Appointment Date: January 4, 2027 Primary Location: Winona, MN Type of Appointment: Administrator/At Will Telework (Yes/No) No About Winona State University Founded in 1858, Winona State University is a regional public university and the oldest member of the Minnesota State system. Offering more than 200 majors and programs, Winona State has the #1 Student Success Rate in the Minnesota State System with 96.97 percent of WSU graduates being hired in a field related to their degree. U.S. News recognized Winona State as having top-ranking undergraduate programs in nursing, engineering, psychology, business, and computer science. With campuses in both Winona and Rochester, Winona State offers the best of both worlds. Widely known for its stunning natural setting, the Winona campus is nestled between picturesque bluffs and the Mississippi River - meaning rock climbing, paddle-boarding, hiking, and kayaking are within a mile of campus. WSU’s Rochester campus is located in Minnesota’s third largest city - a dynamic hub for industry, arts, and culture, and consistently ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. Winona State University's mission is to enhance the intellectual, social, cultural and economic vitality of the people and communities we serve: a community of learners improving our world. For more information, visit winona.edu. Notice: In accordance with Minnesota State policy, employees driving on university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a motor vehicle records check. The Winona State University Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school's policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security. Three years' worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at https://www.winona.edu/about/safety-security/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security by emailing security@winona.edu . Winona State University is an Equal Opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. A member of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities System. A community of learners improving our world! Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 01-04-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-02-2026 Close Date: 09-29-2026 Posting Contact Name: Robin M Delong Posting Contact Email: rdelong@winona.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/Winona/Associate-Director-of-Scholarships--MSUAASF-Range-C-_JR0000005576": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Scholarships (MSUAASF Range C)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Associate Director of Scholarships (MSUAASF Range C) Institution: Winona State University Classification Title: MSUAASF Range C Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: Winona FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $47,845.00 - $93,809.00 Job Description   The Associate Director of Scholarship manages the university’s Foundation Scholarship Program to ensure effective scholarship program administration. Responsibilities include participating in the development of scholarships (including working with the fundraising staff on criteria, writing of drafts, ensuring award-ability and input into the software), managing the scholarship software, developing communications, supporting students through the application and awarding process, and providing guidance to application reviewers. The position builds and maintains collaborative relationships across the division, with campus partners such as Financial Aid and Admissions, and with external stakeholders advance the university’s scholarship strategy. Responsibilities: 1. Scholarship System. Serve as the university expert for the award management software and direct the university's utilization of the tool. Make sure all new scholarship agreements are executed and uploaded. Guide stakeholders on how to utilize the software to administer scholarship dollars. Ensure scholarship system data accurately reflects awarding parameters agreed upon with benefactors. Utilize the system to advertise and process recruitment and other university scholarships. Provide training and guidance to support application reviews and award offers. Serve as the liaison with WSU IT and the scholarship software vendor to troubleshoot and integrate enhancement in the system.   2. Scholarship Strategy . Manage the scholarship program to maximize utilization of student scholarship funds. Collaborate with Advancement team members and benefactors to develop and implement scholarships that meaningfully represent the benefactors’ philanthropic goals and adhere to applicable policies, procedures and laws. Promote the scholarship program to students, parents, and other stakeholders, including Admissions, Financial Aid, Equity and Inclusive Excellence, and academic departments. Ensure scholarship application evaluators are identified, trained, and complete application reviews. Collaborate with other departments to gather and share sensitive information necessary to verify student eligibility. Support the WSU Foundation Scholarship Committee by supporting committee operations, including agenda development, meeting scheduling, minute preparation, and follow-up on action items. Creation of the scholarship documents with input from the fundraising staff. Maintaining the hard copies of the executed scholarship documents. Assist with the annual allocation from each scholarship with the Foundation Controller, Executive Director and the VP of University Advancement. 3. Stewardship and Donor Engagement. Develop and maintain relationships to support scholarship award sustainability and growth. Provide guidance to prospective donors acting as a gatekeeper for WSU fundraising team. Ensure scholarship benefactors receive individualized recognition and expressions of gratitude from the university. Example would be the student thank you initiative. Foster meaningful connections between scholarship recipients and benefactors through letters, events, classroom speaking opportunities, and other engagement activities including an annual scholarship event. Represent the division at key events that promote donor engagement.   4. S cholarship Budget. Maintain budget and data needs related to the scholarship plan. Communicate with the Foundation Controller to ensure adequate funding is available prior to posting available scholarships. Collaborate with the Executive Director to contact benefactors to solicit additional contributions or obtain guidance regarding awarding preferences in cases of insufficient funding. Collaborate with the Executive Director, Controller and VP of Advancement to use data-informed decision-making in the awarding and disbursement of scholarships. Collaborate with the Controller to monitor expenditures and maintain monthly records of endowment and account balances to ensure responsible stewardship of dollars. 5. Emergency Grant Program. Collaborate with the university emergency grant program administrator. Be the liaison between the university emergency grant administrator and the WSU Foundation. 6. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the smooth functioning of the department and maintain the reputation of Winona State University. Including but not limited to participating in university committees and pursuing ongoing professional development to maintain current knowledge in the field. Salary Range: $ 47,845-$93,809; Commensurate with qualifications and experience Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Two (2) years of professional experience in customer relations, marketing, fundraising, student development or enrollment services. Strong oral, written interpersonal and electronic communication skills sufficient to prepare messages and materials for diverse audiences and clearly explain, discuss, and present. Technical skills to efficiently process electronic workflows, maintain data, and generate reports. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion.   Preferred Qualification  Experience using Award Management or related student aid software. Experience developing scholarship strategies that convey the university’s mission. Experience in higher education or non-profit organization. Experience with databases and records management, spreadsheets and benchmarking techniques. Successful experience in developing, documenting, and presenting cultivation and solicitation strategies/proposals.   Other Requirements 1. The successful candidate must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States by the day employment begins. The University regrets that we are unable to offer H1-B sponsorship at this time 2. A complete online application will include the following: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed previously Current Curriculum Vitae / Resume Transcripts (undergraduate and graduate) A list of professional references with contact information   Posting Information: Application Deadline: Review begins September 16, 2026 Appointment Date: As Soon As Possible Primary Location: Winona, MN Type of Appointment: Probationary Telework (Yes/No) No About Winona State University Founded in 1858, Winona State University is a regional public university and the oldest member of the Minnesota State system. Offering more than 200 majors and programs, Winona State has the #1 Student Success Rate in the Minnesota State System with 96.97 percent of WSU graduates being hired in a field related to their degree. U.S. News recognized Winona State as having top-ranking undergraduate programs in nursing, engineering, psychology, business, and computer science. With campuses in both Winona and Rochester, Winona State offers the best of both worlds. Widely known for its stunning natural setting, the Winona campus is nestled between picturesque bluffs and the Mississippi River - meaning rock climbing, paddle-boarding, hiking, and kayaking are within a mile of campus. WSU’s Rochester campus is located in Minnesota’s third largest city - a dynamic hub for industry, arts, and culture, and consistently ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. Winona State University's mission is to enhance the intellectual, social, cultural and economic vitality of the people and communities we serve: a community of learners improving our world. For more information, visit winona.edu. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for Minnesota State University Association of Administrative & Service Faculty (ASF) which can be found at https://www.minnstate.edu/system/working/relations.html Notice: In accordance with Minnesota State policy, employees driving on university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a motor vehicle records check. The Winona State University Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school's policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security. Three years' worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at https://www.winona.edu/about/safety-security/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security by emailing security@winona.edu . Winona State University is an Equal Opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. A member of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities System. A community of learners improving our world! Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-16-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-24-2026 Close Date: 09-17-2026 Posting Contact Name: Robin M Delong Posting Contact Email: rdelong@winona.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Minnesota_State_Careers/job/Winona/Assistant-Professor-of-Data-Science-or-Statistics_JR0000005424": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Data Science or Statistics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant Professor of Data Science or Statistics Institution: Winona State University Classification Title: State University Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: Winona FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $64,963.00 - $193,146.00 Job Description Teach a variety of data science and statistics courses primarily in an in-person format. Instruct courses in varied locations, at varied times, and via various media commensurate with department and university needs. Engage in scholarly research or creative achievement to enhance knowledge of data science or statistics. Provide evidence of continuing preparation and study in the field to enhance teaching abilities. Contribute to student growth and development including student advising. Provide service to the university and community including the program, the department, the college, the university, and the greater community. Support Winona State University's mission to enhance the intellectual, social, cultural, and economic vitality of the people and communities we serve. Teach courses using an innovative and modern curriculum. Contribute to the continued improvement of the curriculum in data science and statistics. Supervise capstone experiences, e.g. student research projects, internships, etc.   Salary Range: $64,963 - $193,146; commensurate with qualifications and experience Minimum Qualifications Ph.D in Data Science, Statistics, or Biostatistics with an anticipated completion date before August 2027. Experience teaching an undergraduate data science or statistics course as the primary instructor or as a teaching assistant.   Preferred Qualification  Skills/ability to integrate technology to enhance learning and teaching. Demonstrated commitment to quality teaching. Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Demonstrated excellence in the teaching of data science or statistics at the undergraduate level as the primary instructor. Evidence of a commitment to continually improve the data science or statistics curriculum Ability to make connections with industry partners, recruit students, develop workshops, and promote our disciplines to high school students. Experience in the applications of data science or statistics. Proficiency in a variety of programming languages such as Python, R, and SQL. Desire to teach Python programming in our upper-division data science courses. Experience with one or more of the following areas: machine learning, consulting, healthcare analytics, or research in the teaching and learning of data science or statistics. Evidence of strong communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work cooperatively with colleagues. Other Requirements 1. The successful candidate must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States by the day employment begins. The University regrets that we are unable to offer H1-B sponsorship at this time. 2. A complete online application will include the following: A cover letter that addresses the qualifications listed previously Current Curriculum Vitae / Resume Transcripts (undergraduate and graduate) A list of professional references with contact information At least three (3) letters of reference.Please advise persons providing letters of reference of Minnesota’s open record law which can make such letters available to applicants upon request.Letters can be sent to jobs@winona.edu.   Posting Information: Application Deadline: Review of applications begins October 15, 2026 Appointment Date: August 16, 2027 Primary Location: Winona, Minnesota Type of Appointment: Probationary/Tenure-Track Telework (Yes/No) No About The Department The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Winona State University offers undergraduate degrees in mathematics, data science, mathematics education, and statistics.  The Department includes a total of 17 faculty members who are responsible for teaching a wide variety of lower-division and upper-division courses.  Winona State University has consistently earned a spot on the Princeton Review’s coveted “Best in the Midwest” list - Winona State is the only university in the Minnesota State Colleges and University system to make this list.  For more information about our department and our mathematics program, see https://www.winona.edu/academics/colleges/science-engineering/mathematics-statistics-department/   About Winona State University Founded in 1858, Winona State University is a regional public university and the oldest member of the Minnesota State system. Offering more than 200 majors and programs, Winona State has the #1 Student Success Rate in the Minnesota State System with 96.97 percent of WSU graduates being hired in a field related to their degree. U.S. News recognized Winona State as having top-ranking undergraduate programs in nursing, engineering, psychology, business, and computer science. With campuses in both Winona and Rochester, Winona State offers the best of both worlds. Widely known for its stunning natural setting, the Winona campus is nestled between picturesque bluffs and the Mississippi River - meaning rock climbing, paddle-boarding, hiking, and kayaking are within a mile of campus. WSU’s Rochester campus is located in Minnesota’s third largest city - a dynamic hub for industry, arts, and culture, and consistently ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. Winona State University's mission is to enhance the intellectual, social, cultural and economic vitality of the people and communities we serve: a community of learners improving our world. For more information, visit winona.edu. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Inter Faculty Organization (IFO) which can be found at https://www.minnstate.edu/system/working/relations.html Notice: In accordance with Minnesota State policy, employees driving on university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a motor vehicle records check. The Winona State University Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school's policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security. Three years' worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at https://www.winona.edu/about/safety-security/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security by emailing security@winona.edu . Winona State University is an Equal Opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. A member of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities System. A community of learners improving our world! Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 08-16-2027 Position End Date: Open Date: 07-23-2026 Close Date: 10-31-2026 Posting Contact Name: Robin M Delong Posting Contact Email: rdelong@winona.edu"
